+# Online matchmaking patch (exvs2-lobbies) — EXPERIMENTAL, NOT WORKING IN-GAME YET
+
+> ⚠️ This branch has **never been tested with the real game**. Everything is based on static analysis of the
+> IB exe ([exvs2-lobbies](https://github.com/ServerOmega/exvs2-lobbies)) and on fake-cabinet tests.
+> You must already have a copy of the game. Upstream: Chiang-17/EXVS2-IB-Server (v1.2.0, commit 7f4b280).
+
+## What this changes
+| Area | Upstream | This patch |
+|---|---|---|
+| RegisterPcb | SRV_MATCH `"{host}/match"`, no STUN | when `OnlineMatching.Enabled`: SRV_MATCH = full URL (`MatchUrl` or `http://{host}/match`) + **SRV_STUN** entry (`StunHost`/`StunPort`) |
+| MMS `/match` (`/mms` alias) | Ping, IssueNodeId → `[1]`, MatchingSetting; everything else `ERR_SERVER` | IssueNodeId → unique persisted ids (≥ issue_count); **EntryMatching / CheckMatching / CancelMatching** with an in-memory 2v2 matchmaker |
+| Matchmaker | — | per-mode queues (world id + attrs), solo shuffle, fixed pairs never split, CPU stand-ins, ranked (worlds 13/14) bucketed by class with level band widening 0→1→2→any at 0/15/35/60 s, blacklists, optional 1v1/2v1 after `FillAfterSeconds` |
+| LoadClassMatch | 1 unix-time schedule row, empty pattern & search-ratio tables | hour row (0–27) **and** unix row → pattern 1; grade→level pattern rows for classes 1–4; search ratios; request table |
+| SaveVsmOnResult | badge only | also stores Class Match `after_rate`, class, grade and class win/lose (OMM_CLASS) |
+| PreLoadCard | `grade_solo/team` always 0 | returns the stored grade |
+| DB | — | migration `AddClassMatchGrade` (adds `Grade` to both class-record tables) |
+| Build | Windows only | optional Linux build: `-p:LinuxHost=true` (drops the WinForms disclaimer dialog) |
+
+## Build
+```
+# Windows (as upstream):           dotnet publish Server-Infinite -c Release -r win-x64
+# Linux host:                      dotnet build Server-Infinite -p:LinuxHost=true -o out && cd out && dotnet Server-Infinite.dll
+# Cross-check Windows build on Linux: dotnet build Server-Infinite -p:EnableWindowsTargeting=true -r win-x64
+# Matchmaker unit tests:           dotnet test Tests/Matchmaking.Tests
+```
+.NET 9 SDK required. Note `.gitignore` excludes `wwwroot/` image resources (needed only for the web UI).
+
+## Configure (`Configurations/server.json` → `CardServerConfig.OnlineMatching`)
+```json
+"OnlineMatching": {
+  "Enabled": true,
+  "MatchUrl": "",              // "" = built-in MMS at http://<host the cabinet used>/match
+                               // or e.g. "http://203.0.113.10:5000/mms" for the external Python server
+  "StunHost": "203.0.113.10",  // coturn; IP literal recommended ("" = same host as this server)
+  "StunPort": 3478,
+  "StunUser": "", "StunPass": "",
+  "PollingIntervalSeconds": 3,
+  "FillAfterSeconds": 30, "AllowPartialRooms": true,
+  "ClassMatchScheduleMode": "Both"   // Both | Hours | UnixTime
+}
+```
+Environment overrides also work, e.g. `CardServerConfig__OnlineMatching__Enabled=true`.
+Cabinet side: `battleMode: 0` in the active `testmode_pcb.json` entry (online path instead of the LM).
+
+## Known gaps / risks
+* Hole-punch / P2P packet format unknown; real battles need reachable UDP (public IP/UPnP or a shared VPN).
+* Mode→world mapping, class ids (1–4) and the hour-based schedule are inferred, not observed.
+* `Grade1Solo/Team`, promotion matches, Extreme ladder (`LoadRankMatch`) untouched.
+* Hand-written migration has no Designer file (EF applies it; snapshot updated).
+* Matchmaker state is in memory; restart drops waiting players (node ids persist).
